CAT = "nzreDisclosure"; SEG = "DSC"
Q = [
("A salesperson wants to buy a house their agency is selling. What does section 134 require first?",
 "Client's consent", ["Agent's written consent", "Discount from the vendor", "Authority's consent"],
 "Section 134 bars a licensee from acquiring the land, directly or through a partner or nominee, without the consent of the client for whom they act."),
("A salesperson arranges for their brother to buy a client's house, without telling the client. What does section 134(2) restrict?",
 "Carrying on the sale", ["Only paying the brother's costs", "Only advertising the sale", "Nothing, relatives are exempt"],
 "Section 134(2) bars a licensee from carrying out or continuing agency work, without the client's consent, if the transaction will or is likely to result in a related person acquiring the land."),
("A client's consent to a licensee buying their property is effective only if it is given in the prescribed form and:",
 "A valuation is provided", ["A lawyer witnessed it", "Agent counter-signed", "The Authority has been told"],
 "Section 134(3) makes the client's consent effective only if in the prescribed form and the client is provided with a valuation under section 135."),
("A licensee buys a client's land in breach of section 134. What may the client do?",
 "Cancel and recover commission", ["Only claim a partial refund", "Only complain to the agent", "Nothing once it has settled"],
 "Under section 134(4) to (6) the client may cancel a contract made in breach, no commission is payable, and any commission paid can be recovered as a debt."),
("Who must make the valuation given to a client under section 135 for a land transaction?",
 "Independent registered valuer", ["Licensee's own manager", "Client's lawyer", "Council's rating valuer"],
 "Section 135 requires the valuation to be made by an independent registered valuer (or, for a business, an independent qualified statutory accountant), at the licensee's expense."),
("Who pays for the section 135 valuation?",
 "Licensee", ["Client", "Authority", "Buyer"],
 "Section 135(1) says the licensee must give the client a valuation made at the licensee's expense."),
("When must the licensee provide the valuation under section 135?",
 "Before consent, or within 14 days", ["Within 28 days of consent", "Only after consent is signed", "Within 48 hours of the sale"],
 "Section 135(3) says the valuation must be given either before seeking the client's consent or, with the client's agreement, within 14 days after obtaining it."),
("Which person counts as \"related to the licensee\" for sections 134 to 136?",
 "Licensee's grandchild", ["Client's neighbour", "Licensee's cousin", "Close friend of the licensee"],
 "Section 137 includes partners, employees, engaged branch managers and salespersons, spouse, civil union or de facto partner, and a child, grandchild, brother, sister, nephew or niece of the licensee or partner."),
("Under section 136, a licensee must tell each prospective party in writing:",
 "Whether they or kin may benefit", ["Licensee's commission rate", "Agency's other listings", "Any past complaints against them"],
 "Section 136 requires written disclosure to every prospective party of whether the licensee, or a person related to the licensee, may benefit financially from the transaction."),
("By when must the section 136 benefit disclosure be made?",
 "Before or when contract papers are given", ["Within 14 days after signing", "At the final settlement day", "Only if the buyer later asks"],
 "Section 136(3) says the disclosure must be made before or at the time the licensee provides the prospective party with any contractual documents."),
("An agent earns commission on a sale. Does the commission alone count as a financial benefit that must be disclosed under section 136?",
 "No, commission alone is excluded", ["Yes, in every case it arises", "Yes, if it is over the usual rate", "Yes, for sole agencies only"],
 "Section 136(4) says an agent does not benefit financially from a transaction merely because of commission payable under an agency agreement."),
("A house has an unrepaired leak the salesperson has seen. What does rule 10.7 require?",
 "Tell customers of the defect", ["Silence unless a customer asks", "Disclosure only after the sale", "Note on the file only"],
 "Rule 10.7 says a licensee is not required to discover hidden defects but must disclose known defects to a customer."),
("The Rules say a licensee need not discover hidden defects. A licensee who sees a likely risk must still:",
 "Seek proof or warn the customer", ["Wait until the buyer's inspection", "Ask the council to inspect it", "Tell the vendor to decide"],
 "Where hidden defects would appear likely to a reasonably competent licensee, rule 10.7 requires confirmation from the client supported by evidence or expert advice, or informing the customer of the significant risk."),
("A client tells a salesperson to keep a known defect from buyers. Under rule 10.8, the licensee:",
 "Must stop working for them", ["May continue if the client signs", "May continue after a written warning", "May continue if the buyer waives it"],
 "Rule 10.8 says a licensee must not continue to act for a client who directs that information about known or likely defects be withheld."),
("The Rules say a customer is expected to inquire into a property. Can a licensee therefore rely on caveat emptor?",
 "No, not simply", ["Yes, always", "Yes, in rural sales", "Yes, if the buyer has a lawyer"],
 "The note to rule 10.7 says a licensee must not simply rely on caveat emptor, even though customers are expected to inspect and take advice."),
("Under rule 10.2, an appraisal of land must be:",
 "Written, realistic, backed by sales", ["Given verbally to keep it short", "Based on the vendor's own hopes", "Set at the latest council valuation"],
 "Rule 10.2 requires a written appraisal that realistically reflects current market conditions and is supported by comparable information on sales of similar land in similar locations."),
("There are no comparable sales for a unique property. What must the licensee do?",
 "Explain this to the client in writing", ["Use the highest sale in the suburb", "Skip the appraisal", "Quote the rating valuation instead"],
 "Rule 10.3 says where no directly comparable or semi-comparable sales data exists, the licensee must explain this in writing to the client."),
("A vendor wants a price expectation that is far above the appraisal. Rule 10.4 says the advertised price must:",
 "Reflect the agreed pricing", ["Match the top rival listing", "Be set by the agent alone", "Match the latest council valuation"],
 "Rule 10.4 says an advertised price must clearly reflect the pricing expectations agreed with the client. Rule 9.4 bars misleading customers about those expectations."),
("A licensee tells buyers the vendor will \"take offers over $600,000\" knowing the vendor expects far more. Which rule does this breach?",
 "Misleading customers on price", ["Rule on record keeping", "Rule on commission", "Rule on trust accounts"],
 "Rule 9.4 says a licensee must not mislead customers as to the price expectations of the client."),
("A property's LIM shows it sits in a flood zone, and the salesperson has the LIM. What is expected?",
 "Read it, flag material issues", ["Hand it on without reading it", "Wait for the buyer to raise it", "Treat it as the vendor's problem"],
 "REA guidance says a licensee who holds a LIM must read and understand it and communicate material issues to prospective buyers, not just act as a conduit."),
("A vendor mentions an unconsented garage conversion. What is the licensee's position?",
 "They must meet their disclosure duties", ["They may ignore it as it is the owner's matter", "They may disclose it only if asked", "They should leave it for the buyer's lawyer"],
 "REA material says if a licensee is aware of unpermitted or non-consented alterations, they must meet their disclosure obligations."),
("A buyer's agent is authorised on certain terms. May the agent do agency work on different terms with other parties?",
 "No, only on authorised terms", ["Yes, if it helps close a deal", "Yes, if the vendor's agent agrees", "Yes, if the customer agrees"],
 "Rule 11.3 says a licensee must not undertake agency work with customers or other licensees on terms different from those authorised by the client."),
("A licensee advertises a property at a price different from the one the client authorised. Which rule does this breach?",
 "Rule on advertising terms", ["Rule on trust account money", "Rule on written appraisals", "Rule on copies of offers"],
 "Rule 10.9 says a licensee must not advertise land or a business on terms different from those authorised by the client."),
("Under section 134(7), when a salesperson's work enables the agent to act for a vendor, the vendor is also:",
 "Salesperson's client", ["Only the agent's client", "Customer of the salesperson", "No one's client"],
 "Section 134(7) says the client of an agent is also the client of any branch manager or salesperson whose work enables the agent to do agency work, so the acquisition restrictions apply to them too."),
]
